course: dictionary
lesson: 9243
title: Sore: pain, a spot, and more
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Sore is a word with more than one meaning. Read the words around it to find out which one fits. «Most sore throats get better by themselves in a few days» is about pain, because a throat that hurts is sore.
explain: Sore can also be a noun. «Tell a grown-up about a blister early and cover it with a plaster, before it becomes an open sore.» Here a sore is a painful spot on the skin. Try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Sore can mean upset, too, especially in American talk. «Sorry, I was being a sore loser» means Chloe was cross when she was losing. Her sore feelings are about the game, not her body.
fact: Sore can be an adjective (sorer, sorest) or a noun (a sore, sores).
fact: Sore means painful, aching or tender, especially when touched or used.
fact: A sore is a painful spot on the skin, often red or broken.
fact: In informal American English, sore means upset or annoyed.
fact: A sore point is a subject that upsets someone.
exercise: «Most sore throats get better by themselves in a few days with drinks and rest.» What does sore mean here? | Really hungry | Very loud and noisy | *Painful and aching | Happy and full of energy
exercise: «Tell a grown-up about a blister early, before it becomes an open sore.» What is a sore in this sentence? | A loud noise from a drum | A soft kind of bread | *A painful spot on the skin | A kind of game
exercise: «Sorry, I was being a sore loser.» What is a sore loser? | Someone who never plays games | *Someone who gets angry when they lose | A player with a sore arm | Someone who wins every time
test: «A sore arm after a jab is a normal sign the immune system is responding.» What does sore mean here? | Loud and cheerful | Upset or annoyed | Very hungry | *Aching or tender
test: Ben says, «That was a sore point for him.» What is a sore point? | A point scored in a game | *A subject that upsets someone | A sharp point on a pencil | A spot on the skin
exam: In «She has a cold sore on her lip», what does sore mean? | Painful in the muscles | Tired from sport | Upset or annoyed | *A painful spot on the skin
